            "kind": "execute",
            "raw_output": "246:def inverse_transform_single_channel(data, mean, std, sl_scale_factor, epsilon):\n324:    forecast targets for temporal prediction tasks. Handles variable input\n343:        time_delta_target_minutes: Step size in minutes between forecast frames.\n345:            Only used when ``load_forecast_frames=True``.\n348:        rollout_steps: Number of additional forecast steps beyond the first target frame.\n350:            Only used when ``load_forecast_frames=True``.\n389:        load_forecast_frames: If True (default), load both input and forecast frames and include\n390:            ``forecast`` and ``lead_time_delta`` in the returned sample. Set to False for downstream\n423:        load_forecast_frames: bool = True,\n448:        self.load_forecast_frames = load_forecast_frames\n529:        When ``load_forecast_frames=False``, only input-frame offsets are checked, so the\n532:        if self.load_forecast_frames:\n567:    def __getitem__(self, idx: int) -> dict:\n578:            When ``load_forecast_frames=True`` (default), also includes:\n579:                forecast (np.ndarray):         (C, L, H, W) \u2014 target frames\n580:                lead_time_delta (np.ndarray):  (L,) \u2014 lead times in hours (negative = future)\n582:                input_latitudes (list[float])\n583:                forecast_latitude (list[float])  \u2014 only when ``load_forecast_frames=True``\n638:            \"ts\": stacked_inputs,\n642:        if self.load_forecast_frames:\n645:            sample[\"forecast\"] = self._load_and_stack_frames(target_timesteps)\n646:            sample[\"lead_time_delta\"] = (\n651:            sample[\"ts\"] = np.flip(sample[\"ts\"], axis=-2).copy()\n652:            if self.load_forecast_frames:\n653:                sample[\"forecast\"] = np.flip(sample[\"forecast\"], axis=-2).copy()\n658:            sample[\"input_latitudes\"] = [get_earth(ts).lat.value for ts in input_timesteps]\n659:            if self.load_forecast_frames:\n660:                sample[\"forecast_latitude\"] = [get_earth(ts).lat.value for ts in target_timesteps]\n896:    def transform_data(self, data: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n912:    def inverse_transform_data(self, data: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\nShell cwd was reset to /home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/flare_forecast/old-chats-notebooks",
