      "body": "Plan written. Here's the short version.\n\n**Yes, `HelioSpectformer2D` is right** \u2014 and it already exists in `workshop_infrastructure/models/finetune_models.py:228`. Nothing new to build there.\n\n**Why your cell 17 blows up**\n- `HelioSpectformer2D.__init__` (`finetune_models.py:238`) has no `num_outputs` parameter \u2192 `TypeError` from `cls(**kwargs)` inside `from_config`.\n- `num_outputs` is a *1D* concept (\"how many scalars to regress\"). The 2D head's knobs are `ft_out_chans` (how many image channels) and `ft_unembedding_type`.\n- The structural difference: the backbone returns tokens `(B, 65536, 1280)`. The 1D head pools those 65536 away to a scalar. The 2D head (`LinearDecoder`, `embedding.py:130`) reshapes them into a 256\u00d7256 token grid and pixel-shuffles back up to `(B, ft_out_chans, 4096, 4096)`.\n\n**Your config already defines a real 2D task** \u2014 no YAML change needed. `time_delta_input_minutes: [-60, -36]` + `time_delta_target_minutes: 0` means: inputs at T\u221260 and T\u221236, target at T. Since helio.py treats the *last* input offset as \"now\", that's a genuine **36-minute-ahead forecast** of the full 13-channel stack.\n\n**The finding that matters most.** I dumped the checkpoint. `surya.366m.v1.pt` contains `unembed.unembed.0.weight` with shape `(3328, 1280, 1, 1)` \u2014 and 3328 = 16\u00b2 \u00d7 13, i.e. it *is* exactly the `LinearDecoder` your 2D head builds. But `load_pretrained_weights` only tries the keys `k` and `backbone.{k}`, never `head_{k}`, so it silently drops the decoder and your head starts random. It reports `157 / 159`.\n- One-line fix in `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py:404` \u2192 `159 / 159`, and your very first plot shows a real Sun instead of noise. Without it you're fitting a random readout and the plot stays garbage for a long time.\n\n**Three more errors waiting after cell 17** \u2014 all in the plan with cell numbers:\n- `FlareLightningModule` builds `target = batch[\"forecast\"].unsqueeze(1)` \u2192 `(B,1,13,1,4096,4096)`, which mismatches the model output. Needs a 2D variant (target is `batch[\"forecast\"][:, :, 0]`).\n- Cells 25/34 import from `downstream_apps.template.*` instead of your own `flare_forecast` copies.\n- Cells 28/30/32 reference an `output` that's never defined (cell 23 is commented out).\n\nGood news: `FlareMetrics` already does `reshape(-1)` on both arguments, so it works on images unchanged \u2014 no new metrics file.\n\nTwo things I'd fix in the same pass but that aren't blocking, both flagged in the plan: your LoRA `target_modules` lists HuggingFace names (`q_proj`, `out_proj`, \u2026) that **don't exist in Surya**, so attention is silently never adapted; and `flip_probability` currently isn't forwarded by `build_helio_dataloaders` at all, and when it is, it flips input *and* target together \u2014 augmentation, not an un-flip task.\n\nFor the plot itself I'll reuse the `_show`/`_lim` helpers you already wrote in `0_dataset_TEST-2.ipynb` cell 21, laid out as **input t\u221260 \u00b7 input t\u221236 \u00b7 ground truth \u00b7 prediction \u00b7 difference**, in physical units via `inverse_transform_data`.\n\nOne thing to flag: this box is an **L40S with 46 GB**, not an 80 GB A100. I'm recommending `ft_out_chans=13` because it's the only value that can reuse the pretrained decoder and the only one `inverse_transform_data` accepts directly \u2014 the plan lists the fallback ladder if it OOMs.",
