                "new_text": "    The pretrained checkpoint was saved from HelioSpectFormer directly, so its keys\n    are flat (e.g. ``embedding.proj.weight``).  The composed fine-tuning models\n    (HelioSpectformer1D, HelioSpectformer2D) nest the backbone under ``backbone.*``,\n    so we try both the original key and the ``backbone.``-prefixed key when matching\n    against the current model's state dict.\n\n    The third spelling tried is ``head_`` + the checkpoint key, which recovers the\n    pretraining *decoder*.  Surya was pretrained with a ``LinearDecoder`` saved under\n    ``unembed.*``, and ``HelioSpectformer2D`` builds exactly that module as\n    ``head_unembed`` -- identical shapes whenever ``ft_out_chans`` equals the channel\n    count the checkpoint was trained on.  Without this candidate the decoder silently\n    fails to match and a 2D fine-tune starts from a randomly initialized readout.\n    The shape check below is what keeps this safe: a head that only *resembles* the\n    pretrained one (a different ``ft_out_chans``, say) is skipped rather than\n    half-loaded.\n\n    Args:\n        model: The fine-tuning model to load weights into.\n        pretrained_path: Path to the pretrained checkpoint (.pt file). No-op if None.\n    \"\"\"",
