      "body": "Let me clear up the confusion first, then deal with the patch \u2014 which actually needs to happen before any of my edits.\n\n**On `head_`: I was adding it, not removing it.** The file I tried to edit was `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py`, in `load_pretrained_weights()` \u2014 a function that has nothing to do with class definitions. It builds a list of key spellings to try when matching checkpoint tensors:\n\n```python\nfor candidate in (k, f\"backbone.{k}\"):     # \u2190 current\nfor candidate in (k, f\"backbone.{k}\", f\"head_{k}\"):   # \u2190 what I proposed\n```\n\nYour `head_` attribute names in the model classes were correct and I wasn't touching them. Sorry that read as the opposite.\n\nBut park that \u2014 your new instructions change the picture, and the upstream patch may well fix this area itself. Let me look at where your repo actually stands."
