      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Yes, it's correct \u2014 and you already have proof. Your cell 45 output shows:\n\n```\nwandb: Currently logged in as: jperei4 (surya-ws2) to https://api.wandb.ai\n```\n\nThat means `cfg.wandb_entity` resolved to the team org and `cfg.wandb_project` resolved fine. Nothing to change.\n\nNotes on the pieces:\n\n- **`log_model=False`** \u2014 keep this. Otherwise wandb uploads your 1.5 GB checkpoint on every improvement. `UploadBestCheckpointToS3` is the intended path for that, and `output.s3_bucket: null` means it's off.\n- **`save_dir=\"./jpereira/wandb/wandb_tmp\"`** \u2014 harmless, just local scratch for wandb's staging files. It gets created for you. Relative to the notebook dir, so it lands in `downstream_apps/flare_forecast/jpereira/...`. Add it to `.gitignore` if it isn't already covered.\n- **`CSVLogger(\"runs\", name=project_name)`** \u2014 writes `./runs/flare_flip_forecast_1/version_N/metrics.csv`. Version number auto-increments per run, so nothing overwrites. Good.\n\n**One thing I'd change:** `run_name` is a fixed string. wandb doesn't dedupe by name, so every re-run creates *another* run also called `flare_flip_finetune_test_1` and you won't be able to tell them apart in the UI \u2014 which is exactly when you need to, since you're about to compare before/after the decoder fix.\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\nrun_name = f\"flare_flip_finetune_{datetime.now():%m%d_%H%M}\"\n```\n\nOr name them for the thing you changed: `\"randomhead_bs2\"` vs `\"pretrainedhead_bs2\"`. That's the comparison you actually care about.",
