      "body": "you're asking me to approve the plan but its written in code so its not easily interpretable by a human--i dont think i understand what the plan is that way. \n\nalso, my flips are literaly vertical flips over the origin (x-axis) as determined by the plots i used to check--i think the sign issue you're mentioning is something we did on purpose. \nthe decoder not being loaded, and the builders issue: idk what this means. the whole point of this experiment is just to see what happens when we use both flipped and not flipped stacks mixed together throughout the whole data (training, validation AND testing). like its to see what happens when we use both \"versions\" of data that can be observed. we're simulating hale's law, with the polarity flips. because we dont have 2 solar cycle's worth of data, we have to use 1 solar cycle and just say that the polarity could be either one way or the other. the goal is to see how the model behaves when we use both kinds of data (flipped or not here means one version of a typical solar cycle or the other). \n\nnone of the info you gave me kind of makes sense to me which is why im asking for more clarity and a better plan moving forward.",
