    {
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "- i understand the plain english explanation and i think i agree that we want all the weights.\n- i do think that we need the \"flipped\" vs \"not flipped\" performance metrics to be different. \n- i did have a question about the prediction image produced... idk how to describe it but basically it just looks \"foggy\" and \"dim\". i wonder if that's because of the \"random numbers\" issue you mentioned? i dont think i fully get why either issue is happening ngl.\n- i dont think i understand how much data goes into the training/validation/testing plan we're coming up with. i don't get how long it'll take VS how much data we're using, etc.... can you clarify? \n- i dont understand what you mean by the final layer is untrained--is that what im trying to figure out with you?\n- i dont think i want to keep getting asked for a code plan when im not ready for that yet. you keep asking me to get approved yet but we need to agree on the plan in words first right?",
      "id": "67a1a56d-b92c-4401-9489-526a3eae4ea3",
      "time": 1789599076.4805813,
      "sender": "jpereira",
      "raw_time": false,
      "metadata": {
        "to_persona": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
